  "worked_solution": "The polar curve $r=4$ is a circle of radius $4$ centered at the origin. It crosses the negative $x$-axis at the point where $r=4$ and $\\theta =\\pi .$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14095706/assets/1e77c7521d2bfd617773666ee6e8cab06442e347382b230f58b00af26a085645.png)\n\nTherefore, the point of intersection in polar coordinates is $(4,\\pi ).$",
